1
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:26,080
Uncle, please let me know
as soon as you get the test results.

2
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,480
I want to know if someone snuck
into Hom Thong's pen that day.

3
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,960
Don't worry about that, Auem.

4
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:35,800
Just focus on paying off the debt.
I'll handle this.

5
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:41,600
Thank you, Uncle.
I'm doing my best right now.

6
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:45,720
But Mom and Orn don't seem
to understand me.

7
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,800
Take it one step at a time, Auem.
I'll be here to help you.

8
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,320
Oh, Auem.

9
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,960
About the DNA test results…

10
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,320
I want you to keep it quiet for now.

11
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,800
I don't want anyone knowing
what we're up to.

12
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:08,759
Because if the DNA test confirms
it's human blood,

13
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:12,200
I'm afraid whoever it belongs to

14
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:15,000
might come after us to silence us.

15
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,480
Okay. In the meantime,

16
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:23,800
I'll make everyone think
I'm only focused on paying off the debt.

17
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,680
Until we find out the truth.

18
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,680
Anyone home?

19
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,040
Anyone here?

20
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,080
Yeah.

21
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,520
Hello, Uncle.

22
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,920
I've got a flat tire.

23
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,080
I was going to call my sister for help,
but my phone died.

24
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,920
Could I charge it at your house?

25
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,400
Sure.

26
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,040
You raise buffaloes too?

27
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,240
Could I take a look?

28
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,920
Weren't you here to charge your phone?
The outlet's on that post.

29
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,760
My family raises buffaloes too.

30
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,920
So I thought I could learn a thing or two.

31
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,680
Mine are called Hom Ngern and Hom Thong.

32
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,440
Are you Yod's son?

33
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,240
You know my father?

34
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,360
I met him at a buffalo competition
a few years ago.

35
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:09,760
How is he?

36
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,200
Is Yod doing well?

37
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,960
My father was hit by a car.
He passed away recently.

38
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,640
Oh, really?

39
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:20,079
I'm sorry to hear that.

40
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,520
What's your buffalo's name?

41
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,960
Chang.

42
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,560
Chang? That's a pretty short name.

43
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,520
Usually, people name their buffaloes
after provinces

44
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,320
or something auspicious, like

45
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,080
Chang Udon, Chang Khon Kaen,

46
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,920
or Chang Billionaire.

47
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,840
People can name them whatever they want.

48
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,720
He's my buffalo.
I'll name him what I like.

49
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,400
Is that coconut oil?

50
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:56,280
My father used to rub it
on our buffaloes' horns too.

51
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,400
It keeps insects and ants away.

52
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,800
What are you doing?

53
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,960
Easy, Uncle. I saw a scorpion.

54
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,760
I was afraid it might sting Por Chang.

55
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,200
Thanks.

56
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,280
What's going on?
What are you doing all the way in here?

57
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:07,160
Oh, I just wanted to see
Por Chang up close.

58
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:11,240
Can I take a picture with Por Chang?

59
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,600
What for?

60
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:18,560
To show my sister
how huge this buffalo is.

61
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,680
-Can I?
-Sure.

62
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,880
Thank you.

63
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,520
Here we go.

64
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,080
Let's take a picture.

65
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,720
CHOK CHAROENSUK FARM

66
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,760
Ob's managed to get close to Tik, boss.

67
00:06:57,480 --> 00:07:00,280
He said he'll keep us updated.

68
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,400
Good.

69
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:06,360
Once he gets Por Chang's semen,
give him 50,000 baht.

70
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:07,680
Yes, sir.

71
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:08,960
What about his sister?

72
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,000
-Here, take a look.
-<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Besides Hom Ngern,</font></font></i>

73
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,600
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">there's Hom Thong too.</font></font></i>

74
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:20,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Look! He ate this grass</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and became a champion.</font></font></i>

75
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:24,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you want your buffalo to be a champion,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">it has to be Yod's Pangola grass.</font></font></i>

76
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:29,000
Auem's making videos about buffaloes
and selling the grass her dad grew.

77
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,120
A million baht in six months?

78
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,360
No way she'll make it.

79
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,280
No, sir.

80
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:47,480
Everyone, Pangola grass
is a long-lived grass.

81
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:51,200
It has thin, hairless stems
and soft leaves.

82
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,320
Pangola grass
is also very high in protein.

83
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,520
It's perfect for feeding
our cattle and buffaloes.

84
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:03,560
Oh! Miki, you're ordering ten packs?

85
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,040
Whoa!

86
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,520
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

87
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:09,320
I'll have Rung take your order
and ship it out tomorrow.

88
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:14,200
How about this?
If anyone sends us a whale gift,

89
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,880
I'll get Auem to play the ukulele

90
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,960
and dance with Hom Ngern. How's that?

91
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,600
-What do you think?
-Din! What are you doing?

92
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:25,160
Auem, someone actually sent a whale!

93
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,320
-Let's go! Whoo!
-Yay!

94
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:31,280
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I've waited so long for you</font></font></i>

95
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:34,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Loving you on my own</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I just want to hold you close</font></font></i>

96
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:38,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Body and soul</font></font></i>

97
00:08:38,159 --> 00:08:40,159
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Tell me not to love you, but I will</font></font></i>

98
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:44,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Tell me not to care, but I will</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">That's just how my heart works</font></font></i>

99
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,880
-Hang on.
-You okay?

100
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,440
-I'm good.
-Okay.

101
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,680
-Easy, easy.
-Okay.

102
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,960
-Yeah.
-Come on.

103
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,680
-One, two.
-Be careful.

104
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,200
Alright.

105
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,720
-Come on. Hurry.
-Let's go.

106
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,920
Quick.

107
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,280
-Come on, Mom.
-Hurry.

108
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,480
ANIMAL FEED

109
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:21,200
We've been livestreaming for a week
and sold 500 packs,

110
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,120
plus 150 bales.

111
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,440
That's over 40,000 baht altogether.

112
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,920
And that's not even counting
the gifts people sent us.

113
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,880
If we can keep selling this much
every week,

114
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,880
I bet we'll make a million baht
within six months, Auem.

115
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,440
Look how much we've made.

116
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:43,400
-Back up! Keep coming!
-Careful.

117
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,320
-Keep backing up!
-Stop!

118
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,200
Stop! Whoa!

119
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,000
Auem, I brought you some stuff.

120
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:58,960
What is it? Why'd you bring so much stuff?

121
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,120
Well,

122
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,920
the organic gardening supplies
I told you about.

123
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,560
I'll teach you to grow organic veggies
so you can earn some extra money.

124
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:12,000
And I've got plenty of dried buffalo dung.
You can sell it on your livestreams.

125
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,440
Thank you, Uncle.

126
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,680
Where are your mom and Orn, dear?

127
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:20,240
I brought some food
so you wouldn't have to buy any.

128
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:23,080
Mom's working at the hair salon.

129
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:26,040
What? Your mom's working?

130
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,400
-Yes.
-Oh!

131
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,560
Goodness!

132
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,840
Hom Ngern, did you hear that, sweetie?

133
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,400
Oh my.

134
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,200
You heard?

135
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:39,080
I was just as shocked
when I first heard it, Auntie.

136
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:48,280
Aunt Sa-Ing! Where are you?
Come out right now!

137
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,400
Go see what's going on.

138
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:59,440
Come out, or we're coming in!

139
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,960
Hey! What's all this about?

140
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:05,120
Hey!

141
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,920
Who are you people?
Why are you barging into someone's home?

142
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,040
We're debt collectors.
Where's Aunt Sa-Ing?

143
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,560
Bring her out here right now!

144
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,880
What debt are you talking about?

145
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,320
-What?
-Hey, grab her!

146
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:22,400
-Hey, wait!
-Let go!

147
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,280
-No!
-Let me go!

148
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,480
Help!

149
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:31,160
Mom, why did you borrow money from them?

150
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:35,840
That's right. She borrowed
30,000 baht from Boss Pon.

151
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:39,120
She promised to pay back 1,000 a day.
It's been five days now,

152
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,040
and he hasn't seen a single baht.

153
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,840
Why did you borrow the money?

154
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:45,920
Orn's concert ticket, right?

155
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:50,600
You borrowed money
to buy Orn a concert ticket?

156
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:59,600
Young man, please calm down.
I'm working at a beauty salon.

157
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:03,600
I only make 600 baht a day.
Give me two or three days to pay you back.

158
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,240
No way! The boss wants his money today.

159
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:09,560
And he said if you don't pay,

160
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,200
we'll take your daughter as interest.

161
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,480
-No! You can't!
-Come here!

162
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,240
-Don't!
-Wait! No!

163
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,280
What are you doing?

164
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,400
-Watch out!
-Hey!

165
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,280
Ob!

166
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,280
Punch him!

167
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,200
Get him!

168
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,840
-Hey!
-Hom Ngern!

169
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:36,960
Hom Ngern!

170
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,520
Auem!

171
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:49,960
I'll pay the debt.

172
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,120
Good.

173
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:02,600
Mom borrowed 30,000,
plus 7,000 in interest, right?

174
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,040
Right.

175
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:08,200
Auem, don't. I'll pay it.

176
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,640
I've transferred the money.

177
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,240
See? That wasn't so hard.
Could've saved yourselves a beating.

178
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,280
Let's go.

179
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:31,280
Sa-Ang, thank you so much.

180
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:32,760
Thank your aunt.

181
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,520
Thank you.

182
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:39,640
Don't thank me. From now on, you two

183
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:43,320
will sell food at school
to work off your debt to me.

184
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,880
No! I'm not doing that!

185
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:48,360
Auem, hurry up and pay her back.

186
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,400
Stop acting like this, Orn.

187
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:55,640
You're the one who made Mom
borrow the money. Take responsibility.

188
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:59,240
But Orn and I never asked you to help.

189
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:01,440
I didn't want to help you either.

190
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,840
I just feel sorry for Auem.

191
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:08,440
What kind of mother are you?
Instead of helping her earn money,

192
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:10,720
you let her work herself to the bone

193
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,440
while you pile up more debt.

194
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:17,520
I just want Orn to be happy.
What's wrong with that?

195
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,640
The problem is you're making
everyone else suffer.

196
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:25,680
Ever since you got married,
you haven't had to work.

197
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,640
You've lived comfortably,

198
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,640
asking Yod for whatever you wanted.

199
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:32,200
And you've spoiled your daughter rotten.

200
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,360
I won't let my niece turn out like you.

201
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,520
Hey.

202
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,280
You're jealous of me, right?

203
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:43,160
Before you met the village headman,
you were a widow.

204
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:44,680
And you had a kid too.

205
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,760
Working yourself to the bone
to raise your child alone.

206
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,600
-Am I right?
-Yes.

207
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:52,400
I used to envy you. But not anymore.

208
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,200
Those hard times taught me
how to earn a living,

209
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:59,960
instead of causing trouble
and being a burden to my child.

210
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,640
-Did you really have to be so harsh?
-Yes!

211
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:04,160
Want me to go on?

212
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,840
So what's it going to be?
Are you going to work or not?

213
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:09,160
Huh?

214
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,160
-If you don't want to work, then don't.
-Yeah.

215
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,600
The concert ticket is in your room, right?

216
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,360
Auem.

217
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,120
Auem! What are you doing?

218
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,080
Auem!

219
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:31,880
Auem, give it back!

220
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,400
-Stop!
-Auem!

221
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:36,560
Auem, give it back!
Give me my ticket back!

222
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,760
Auem!

223
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,680
I said give it back!

224
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,760
Orn.

225
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:44,560
If you won't work, I'll sell the ticket

226
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,920
to pay back Aunt Sa-Ang.

227
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,600
No! You can't sell it, Auem!

228
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,360
-Give it here!
-Fine!

229
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,600
I won't sell it.

230
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:57,640
But Aunt Sa-Ang will hold on to it.
If you want it back, go work for her.

231
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:01,240
I'm your little sister.
You're supposed to be on my side.

232
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,320
If you'd given me the money
in the first place,

233
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,480
Mom and I wouldn't have had
to borrow from anyone.

234
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,000
Orn, stop blaming everyone else.

235
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,480
Get it through your head.
Our family is in debt.

236
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:14,520
So what if we're in debt?
Can't we live normal lives?

237
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,080
-Can't we go out and have fun?
-You can,

238
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,480
but you'll have to earn your own money.

239
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,520
Auem, give it back!

240
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:24,320
Auntie, keep this for me.

241
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,320
Stop!

242
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,120
Ob, let go!

243
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,920
If you want to go to that concert,
you and Mom will have to work for it.

244
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,320
Give it to me, Auntie!

245
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,560
Auntie!

246
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,599
It's okay, Auem.

247
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,359
Things will get better.

248
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:24,680
Thank you so much
for helping us today, Hom Ngern.

249
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:26,720
Don't worry.

250
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:31,600
No matter what happens,
I'll bring Hom Thong back to you.

251
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,560
You understand?

252
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Any update on Uncle Tik?</font></font></i>

253
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:43,600
ANY UPDATE ON UNCLE TIK?

254
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:47,000
-Auem.
-Yeah?

255
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:50,200
Uncle Khwanchai texted me.
Hom Thong isn't feeling well.

256
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,640
I think I'll go stay with him
for a night after school.

257
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,200
Will you make it back in time for school?

258
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:56,880
Of course.

259
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,640
There's a van at 5:30 a.m.
I'll take that one.

260
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,760
Don't worry. I'll be back in time.

261
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,200
Alright.

262
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,640
Eat up.

263
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:18,000
Get out! Back off! I said get out!

264
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,640
I told you I'm not selling!
Stop pestering me!

265
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:21,680
Get out!

266
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:22,640
Please stop.

267
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,320
Uncle, wait! What's going on?

268
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,960
Stay out of this.

269
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,600
Get out! I said get out!

270
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,320
Fine! Don't sell it then!

271
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:31,840
There are plenty of other fine buffaloes
to get semen from.

272
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,920
Yeah! Then go!

273
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,800
And don't come back!

274
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,120
Damn it.

275
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:41,880
What are you doing here?

276
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:44,160
Don't tell me your phone died again.

277
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:51,000
I brought you some snacks to thank you
and a new mosquito net for Chang's pen.

278
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:54,720
I saw the old one was torn.
I was worried mosquitoes might bite him.

279
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:06,960
Why don't you sell his semen, Uncle?

280
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:10,120
I bet Por Chang's semen
would fetch a good price.

281
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:13,240
He's a purebred Uthai buffalo, after all.

282
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:16,600
How do you know he's a purebred Uthai?

283
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,800
My father taught me how to tell.

284
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:30,840
He said buffaloes from Uthai Thani
or the Sakae Krang River basin

285
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:35,960
are known for being tall, long,
broad, and deep-bodied.

286
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,280
And do you know why that is?

287
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,880
In the old days,
villagers raised buffaloes in herds.

288
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:44,000
So Uthai buffaloes

289
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:46,960
ended up breeding with wild buffaloes
around Huai Kha Khaeng.

290
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:51,080
That's why Uthai buffaloes
are bigger than ordinary buffaloes.

291
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:55,080
Yeah, no wonder you're Yod's son.

292
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:59,480
And what makes Por Chang special is that,
besides all those features,

293
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,120
he's an albino buffalo too.

294
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,600
Actually, I think you should consider

295
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:09,720
selling Por Chang's semen.
It would help breed

296
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:11,800
more beautiful giant buffaloes.

297
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:14,320
Why? You want to buy some?

298
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,160
Would you sell me some?

299
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,920
You little rascal.
Want me to chase you off like those guys?

300
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:21,600
No.

301
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:26,320
If I ever decide to sell
Por Chang's semen,

302
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:33,120
I'll only sell it to people
who truly love and care for buffaloes.

303
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,800
Not people who just want
to profit from them.

304
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:48,800
CHOK CHAROENSUK FARM

305
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:03,360
Look, Tik's letting you
get this close to Por Chang now.

306
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:05,800
I think he trusts you, Ob.

307
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:09,800
Next time you go there,
you can drug him with sleeping pills.

308
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:12,040
Sleeping pills, Uncle?

309
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:15,720
Hey, they're just sleeping pills.
They're harmless.

310
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:18,440
Tik won't sell Por Chang's semen

311
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:22,920
because he's afraid people will find out
he stole Sia Aun's buffalo.

312
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,040
Really, Uncle?

313
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,080
Well, of course!

314
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:28,720
All you have to do is put Tik to sleep.

315
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:31,160
Then I'll have the vet and my men

316
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:35,720
bring a female buffalo in heat
to lure Por Chang for semen collection.

317
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:38,040
Got it, Ob?

318
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:51,000
I don't want to do it either, Hom Thong.

319
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:55,360
But I have to help Auem earn enough
to bring you home.

320
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,160
I'm sorry.

321
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:05,800
ANIMAL FEED FOR SALE

322
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:13,120
ANIMAL FEED FOR SALE

323
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,120
Hello.

324
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:24,760
Come on in.

325
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,160
This is your desk, Auem.

326
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,320
And that's Tong and Pang.

327
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,920
Hello.

328
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:39,520
We'll meet at noon to discuss
next week's Mini Farm Fair booth.

329
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:43,120
Tong and Pang will fill you in
on the details.

330
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:45,080
Sure, Mam.

331
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:50,600
Hello, Mam.

332
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:53,240
Can I talk to Auem for a minute?

333
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:54,520
Of course.

334
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,440
I looked into Rut for you.

335
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:03,640
They said he took three days off
because his mother's sick.

336
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,560
Huh?

337
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:07,840
Rut never told me his mother was sick.

338
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:20,440
-We're here.
-Easy, easy.

339
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,600
Why is the house so quiet, Auem?

340
00:23:34,360 --> 00:23:35,440
-Oh!
-Oh!

341
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,480
Auem!

342
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:38,280
-Hello.
-Here to see Rut?

343
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:42,960
Yes. I heard his mother's sick,
so I came to visit her.

344
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:45,720
She's not sick.

345
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:48,720
Boon went to Chiang Mai yesterday
to make merit.

346
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:56,520
-Hold this for me.
-Okay.

347
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,320
AUEMDAO

348
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,360
AUEMDAO, MISSED CALL

349
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:23,800
Why does she keep calling?

350
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:36,760
WHAT IS IT, AUEM? I'M BUSY

351
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I'm outside your mother's house.</font></font></i>

352
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:54,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Someone at the office said she's sick,</font></font></i>

353
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:58,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">so I came to visit.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But Aunt Noi says she's in Chiang Mai.</font></font></i>

354
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:06,760
Answer it.

355
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:11,280
Hello, Auem? You're outside
my house right now?

356
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:13,880
Yes. What's going on, Rut?

357
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:16,600
Is your mother sick,
or is she in Chiang Mai?

358
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:21,760
Well, she's sick in Chiang Mai.

359
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:25,320
That's why I took time off work
to come look after her.

360
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,440
I see.

361
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:31,280
How is she doing now?
Has she seen a doctor?

362
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,240
Yes, she has.

363
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:37,160
I have to go, Auem.
I need to check on Mom.

364
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,520
Wait, Rut.

365
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:42,360
I wanted to talk to you about the gold.

366
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:44,320
Uh…

367
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:48,480
My mother's sick, Auem.
I don't have time to deal with the gold.

368
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:49,760
Rut!

369
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,320
-I have to go now.
-Wait, Rut!

370
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,240
-Mom's calling me.
-Rut!

371
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,560
Woo! Let's go, Mint!

372
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:30,000
Everyone, my father and I
are having CCTV cameras installed.

373
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:32,040
One at the village entrance

374
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:35,680
and another outside Uncle Dang's shop.

375
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:37,520
From now on,

376
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:41,000
if anyone steals our buffaloes again,
we'll know exactly who it is.

377
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:54,480
I've already told Ob
to drug Tik next time.

378
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,520
Good.

379
00:26:56,880 --> 00:27:00,120
I'm getting Por Chang's semen
to breed my buffaloes, no matter what.

380
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:11,600
-Boss.
-Yeah?

381
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,640
-Hello.
-<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Hello, sir.</font></font></i>

382
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:25,880
The villagers complained to Phuyai Dech
about buffaloes going missing lately.

383
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:29,600
So he's having CCTV cameras
installed around the village.

384
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,280
Okay.

385
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:35,360
Boss, the villagers
complained to Phuyai Dech

386
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:37,680
about buffaloes going missing.

387
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:40,440
So he's having CCTV cameras
installed around the village.

388
00:27:40,520 --> 00:27:42,000
Then tell our men

389
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:44,480
to stay away from there for now.

390
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:45,680
Yes, sir.

391
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:57,480
Erng, what do you think?
Is our model pretty enough for you?

392
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:01,720
I saw Auem playing with Hom Ngern,
and I loved it.

393
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:05,320
They're so cute.
I'd love for you to review my products.

394
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:09,320
Of course! What kind
of videos would you like?

395
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:13,720
Just review these supplements.
Make five videos for me.

396
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:16,080
I'll pay you 15,000 baht.

397
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:23,120
Here are the supplement details
and the certificates.

398
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:25,240
My products are completely safe.

399
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,320
Of course.

400
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:30,000
Hom Ngern and I
will make some great videos for you.

401
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,080
Right, Hom Ngern?

402
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:34,400
-Thank you so much, Erng.
-Thank you so much.

403
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:38,200
-Hey, don't be naughty.
-She's being affectionate.

404
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,520
-Auem.
-Huh?

405
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:40,760
Where's my commission?

406
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:45,320
You're charging me now?

407
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:49,120
It doesn't have to be money.
Just treat me to Thai barbecue.

408
00:28:49,840 --> 00:28:52,480
For you? One meatball skewer is enough.

409
00:28:52,560 --> 00:28:54,280
Why are you so stingy?

410
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,120
-Whoa!
-Hey!

411
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,120
Ow!

412
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,040
What's wrong, Auem?

413
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:02,320
Something got in my eye.

414
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:05,080
Let me take a look.

415
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:06,640
Hold on.

416
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,560
-Auem.
-Yeah?

417
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:37,120
Does this arrangement
of vitamin bottles look okay?

418
00:29:38,120 --> 00:29:38,960
Looks good.

419
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:45,280
Wait, aren't Ob and Rung here yet?

420
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:48,400
Rung's helping her mom sell food.
She'll come later.

421
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:52,240
Ob's working on a report with his friends.
He'll probably come later too.

422
00:29:52,320 --> 00:29:53,280
Okay.

423
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:02,120
Hey, Hom Ngern!

424
00:30:02,880 --> 00:30:06,680
Hom Ngern, those bananas
are for filming. Stop that!

425
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:10,680
Auem.

426
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,240
Are you okay, Auem?

427
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:27,120
You came all the way to my house
to check up on me,

428
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:29,840
yet here you are with this buffalo herder?

429
00:30:31,280 --> 00:30:34,240
You've been seeing him
behind my back, haven't you?

430
00:30:34,840 --> 00:30:36,120
No, Rut.

431
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:40,520
Enough, Auem. Stop lying.
I know everything now.

432
00:30:40,600 --> 00:30:42,560
What do you know?

433
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:43,880
You want to know?

434
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:50,320
Here.

435
00:30:57,840 --> 00:30:59,200
You had someone follow me?

436
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:04,280
You've been demanding the gold back
so you can dump me for him, right?

437
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:08,160
Hey, I was just discussing work
with Auem in that photo.

438
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:11,080
Who asked you? Stay out of this.

439
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:13,080
This is between Auem and me.

440
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:17,480
I really didn't want to do this.

441
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:20,000
But since you cheated on me first,

442
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:22,440
I don't have to give your gold back.

443
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:27,120
-What do you mean, Rut?
-Don't you remember our agreement?

444
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:32,840
Here.

445
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:33,800
What's this?

446
00:31:35,080 --> 00:31:38,200
SAVING GOLD, BUILDING LOVE
FOR AUEM AND RUT'S FUTURE

447
00:31:38,280 --> 00:31:40,400
I want us to save up in gold together.

448
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:45,200
Aren't you worried about what'll happen
to the gold if we break up someday?

449
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:47,320
Give me that.

450
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,960
How about this?

451
00:31:57,880 --> 00:32:03,320
"If either of us cheats,
the other gets all the gold."

452
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,360
Okay?

453
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:10,360
If you're okay with it,
why don't you sign?

454
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:13,000
Auemdao.

455
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:14,160
IF EITHER OF US CHEATS
THE OTHER GETS ALL THE GOLD

456
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:18,320
You're the one who broke our agreement.

457
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:20,000
You're the one who cheated first.

458
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:22,920
We're through!

459
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,920
Rut, wait!

460
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:28,080
-Rut!
-Auem!

461
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:33,840
Rut!

462
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,960
-Rut, wait!
-Geez!

463
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:38,360
Listen to me!

464
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:41,000
I really didn't cheat on you.

465
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:43,120
I believe what I saw.

466
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:45,600
Even when you're having problems,
you still turn to him.

467
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:48,880
Because you never have time for me.

468
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:51,960
Ever since my father died,
you haven't answered my calls.

469
00:32:52,040 --> 00:32:55,960
When we do talk, you barely say a word.
And what about Chiang Mai?

470
00:32:56,040 --> 00:32:58,720
Did you really go there
because your mother was sick?

471
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:00,240
And who was that woman I heard?

472
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:03,080
-Don't start picking a fight with me!
-I'm not!

473
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:06,640
I just want to know.
If you went there, show me your ticket.

474
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:10,200
See?

475
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:12,360
Now you're blaming me.

476
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:16,480
If you think I'm such a terrible person,
then it's best we break up.

477
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:19,240
Rut, wait!

478
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:21,560
Let go!

479
00:33:22,360 --> 00:33:23,600
Auem!

480
00:33:27,520 --> 00:33:28,360
Hey!

481
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:29,440
Don't, Hom Ngern!

482
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:33,320
Stay back!

483
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:38,920
Does it hurt a lot, Auem?

484
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:05,240
Rut's seen you with Din plenty of times.

485
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:09,280
Why would he suddenly think
you're cheating on him with Din?

486
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,400
I think he's just looking
for an excuse to break up with me.

487
00:34:13,040 --> 00:34:15,560
Why would Rut want to break up with you?

488
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:17,040
You haven't done anything wrong.

489
00:34:17,120 --> 00:34:19,159
Because I'm in debt, Ob.

490
00:34:20,560 --> 00:34:22,840
Actually, I've felt
he's been acting strange

491
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:25,760
ever since my father died.

492
00:34:25,840 --> 00:34:27,760
And he's been strangely evasive
about the gold.

493
00:34:28,520 --> 00:34:29,760
Exactly.

494
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:33,360
When you're in a relationship,
you're supposed to help each other, right?

495
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:34,280
But look at him.

496
00:34:34,960 --> 00:34:38,639
From what he said earlier,
it sounds like he won't return the gold.

497
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:42,280
What if he's deliberately trying
to cheat you out of it?

498
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:45,280
I don't want to think that either.

499
00:34:46,120 --> 00:34:47,920
But if I haven't done anything wrong,

500
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:50,600
shouldn't I get my share of the gold back?

501
00:34:51,199 --> 00:34:53,800
Then tomorrow, when we go to work
at the Mini Farm Fair,

502
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:58,360
let's ask Rut if he's trying
to cheat you out of the gold.

503
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:05,960
Does it hurt badly? I'm sorry.

504
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:13,680
BUFFALO MILK TOAST

505
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:15,360
BUFFALO MILK DONUT

506
00:35:17,120 --> 00:35:18,360
WANASAWAN FARM

507
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:23,160
WHITE BUFFALO, KOH MUEANG PHET - FARM EXPO

508
00:35:23,240 --> 00:35:27,160
Hello, everyone! Today
at our Chettha Kaset Farm booth,

509
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,200
we have a wide range of products.

510
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:33,240
Animal feed, fertilizers,
various vitamins,

511
00:35:33,320 --> 00:35:35,360
and even bathing products.

512
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:40,360
And best of all, you'll get to meet
Hom Ngern in person.

513
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:42,480
I'll also show you

514
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:46,840
how to mix
my special buffalo feed formula.

515
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:49,640
See you at the Chettha Kaset Farm booth.

516
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:52,480
HOM THONG

517
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:54,240
Auem!

518
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:55,160
Huh?

519
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:59,400
Rut hasn't come by the booth yet,
but I saw his car in the parking lot.

520
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:02,080
I think he's avoiding you on purpose.

521
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:04,720
He can't hide all day.

522
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,400
He has to come to work eventually.

523
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:10,280
If he gives you any trouble,
I'll deal with him.

524
00:36:18,560 --> 00:36:22,360
Auem, look! It's Hom Thong.
Sia Aun brought him here to show off.

525
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:46,200
How are you, Hom Thong?

526
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:48,960
Are you feeling better now?

527
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:54,000
You've grown so much taller, Hom Thong.

528
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:01,880
If you miss each other so much,
better start earning money fast.

529
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:09,280
I hear you've started making money
on TikTok too.

530
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:11,200
Think you can raise enough in six months?

531
00:37:12,120 --> 00:37:15,600
Or would you like me to help
by buying some grass from you?

532
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:17,400
You don't need to worry, Sia Aun.

533
00:37:17,480 --> 00:37:20,040
I'll definitely earn enough
to buy Hom Thong back.

534
00:37:21,080 --> 00:37:24,600
Then you'd better help your sister
earn money too, Ob.

535
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:26,800
So you can get Hom Thong back sooner.

536
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:34,720
Let's take Hom Ngern
back to our booth, Auem.

537
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:43,120
Hang in there a little longer, Hom Thong.

538
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:45,200
I'm doing everything I can to help you.

539
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,200
I feel so sorry
for Hom Ngern and Hom Thong.

540
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:10,880
They must miss each other terribly.

541
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:12,160
Yeah.

542
00:38:14,080 --> 00:38:15,240
Don't worry, Auem.

543
00:38:16,080 --> 00:38:18,160
I'll help you sort things out with Rut.

544
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:19,560
If you get the gold back,

545
00:38:19,640 --> 00:38:21,720
you'll have money
to buy Hom Thong back sooner.

546
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:24,920
But before we can sort this out,

547
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:26,160
we need to find Rut.

548
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,720
We don't even know where he is right now.

549
00:38:29,480 --> 00:38:30,600
Yeah, that's true.

550
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,120
Hom Ngern.

551
00:38:41,200 --> 00:38:42,880
-Hom Ngern!
-Hom Ngern!

552
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:45,200
-Hom Ngern!
-Where are you going?

553
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:46,680
Hom Ngern!

554
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:48,320
-Hom Ngern, wait!
-Hom Ngern!

555
00:38:48,400 --> 00:38:49,720
Hom Ngern!

556
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:51,240
Hom Ngern.

557
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:52,800
What are you doing here?

558
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,160
Huh?

559
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:01,640
MINI FARM FAIR

560
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:06,960
Rut.

561
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:10,000
You look gorgeous today.

562
